    {
      "id": "msg.first_touch.structure",
      "type": "message_rule",
      "owner": "PMM and enablement",
      "version": 1,
      "precedence": 4,
      "status": "active",
      "body": "Follow the Sales handbook's email playbook (05) and Contact Sales handling (03).\nClassify the lead first: Highly Qualified Content, Standard Content, Highly Qualified Code, Standard Code, or the Content price check.\nTCQ: acknowledge the specific request in their message (trigger), connect it to Builder in a sentence (connection), then the ask (question).\nContact Sales is the only source where a meeting belongs in the first touch. Highly Qualified leads get two days for 30 minutes (for example Wednesday or Thursday), no calendar link. Standard leads get 2 or 3 qualifying questions first and a soft offer to find time.\nThe trigger quotes their own words from the message or a form answer; the connection ties it to teams like theirs; the ask is about their world, never their interest in us.\nNever pitch a demo as the first call; call it an intro, walkthrough, or working session.\nNever disclose pricing, except the Content price check. Never invent a fact, metric, or customer quote.\nPlain, casual voice, under 75 words when possible. No em dashes, no colons, a casual sign-off, signed with the owner's first name.\nSay Builder, never Builder.io, Fusion, or Publish. Write in the prospect's language.\n",
      "params": {
        "min_words": 25,
        "target_words": 75,
        "max_words": 130,
        "no_colons": true,
        "banned_chars": [
          "—",
          "–"
        ],
        "banned_terms": [
          "Builder.io",
          "Fusion",
          "Publish"
        ],
        "banned_phrases": [
          "I hope this email finds you well",
          "just circling back",
          "likely under some time pressure",
          "I'm sure you're busy",
          "Best regards",
          "Kind regards",
          "Warm regards",
          "Sincerely",
          "demo our platform",
          "Would you be open to a quick call",
          "What's driving your interest",
          "can help teams",
          "can help you",
          "best-fit",
          "best fit approach",
          "get back to you",
          "our platform",
          "unlock",
          "seamless",
          "leverage",
          "empower",
          "game-changer",
          "cutting-edge",
          "Want to see a demo",
          "Do you have 15 minutes"
        ]
      },
      "source": "Sales handbook, 05 Email playbook and 03 Contact Sales form handling",
      "owner_team": "pa_team",
      "block": "message_rule",
      "section": "messaging",
      "position": 0
    },
    {
